# IC-9700 CI-V command catalog extracted from IC-9700_ENG_CI-V_0.pdf. Format CMD|SUB|DATA|NAME|NOTES
# Default address A2h, controller E0h. Frame FE FE <to> <from> Cn [Sc] [data] FD ; OK=FB, NG=FA. NO 29 receiver prefix on this model: main/sub band selected with 07 D0/D1 (read 07 D2), unselected VFO via cmd 25/26.
# Asterisks in manual: * = send/read; *1 read only; *2 send only; *3 CW msg sent in CW mode with TX/break-in; *4 power ON (18 01) needs FE preamble (4800:5, 9600:9, 19200:20, 38400:40, 57600:59, 115200:119); *5 memory keyer counter: clear other channel's counter first; *6 set at least 1 GPS sentence ON (max 4); *7 output setting auto OFF after power OFF; *8 USB port needs CI-V USB Port=Unlink from REMOTE and CI-V Baud=115200 (LAN port always ok)
# FREQ = BCD 5 bytes LSB first: [10Hz 1Hz][1kHz 100Hz][100kHz 10kHz][10MHz 1MHz][1GHz 100MHz] (10MHz digit 0-9, 1GHz digit 0-1, 100MHz digit 0-4)
00||FREQ BCD 5 bytes (see p.13)|Send the frequency data (transceive)|
01||MODE bytes (see p.13)|Send the mode data (transceive)|
02||BAND EDGE (see p.13)|Read the band edge frequencies|read only (*1)
03||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Read the operating frequency|read only (*1)
04||MODE 2 bytes mode,filter|Read the operating mode|read only (*1)
05||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Set the operating frequency|send only (*2)
06||MODE bytes mode[,filter]|Set the operating mode|send only (*2); mode 00 LSB,01 USB,02 AM,03 CW,04 RTTY,05 FM,07 CW-R,08 RTTY-R,17 DV,22 DD (DD selectable in 1200 MHz band other than satellite mode); filter 01 FIL1,02 FIL2,03 FIL3 may be skipped
07||(none)|Select the VFO mode|
07|00||Select VFO A|in satellite mode: selects the VFO mode
07|01||Select VFO B|in satellite mode FA (NG) is returned
07|A0||Equalize VFO A and VFO B|
07|B0||Exchange MAIN and SUB Bands|
07|D0||Select the main band|
07|D1||Select the sub band|
07|D2|00 or 01|Send/read main/sub band selection|send/read (*); 00=main band selection 01=sub band selection
08||(none)|Select the Memory mode|send only (*2)
08||BCD 2 bytes 0001 to 0099|Select the Memory channel (including satellite mode)|0001=M-CH01 0099=M-CH99
08||BCD 2 bytes 0100 to 0105|Select program scan edge channel 1A/1B to 3A/3B|0100/0101 (1A ch/1B ch) ... 0104/0105 (3A ch/3B ch)
08||BCD 2 bytes 0106, 0107|Select call channel C1/C2|0106=C1 0107=C2
09||(none)|Memory write|
0A||(none)|Memory copy to VFO|
0B||(none)|Memory clear|
0C||see p.13|Read frequency offset (duplex offset)|read only (*1)
0D||see p.13|Send frequency offset|send only (*2)
0E|00||Cancel the scan|
0E|01||Start a Programmed/memory scan|
0E|02||Start a Programmed scan|
0E|03||Start a F scan|
0E|12||Start a Fine programmed scan|
0E|13||Start a Fine F scan|
0E|22||Start a Memory scan|
0E|23||Start a Select memory scan|
0E|24||Start a Mode Select scan|
0E|A1~A7||Select F scan span|send only (*2); x=1..7: +-5,+-10,+-20,+-50,+-100,+-500 kHz,+-1 MHz
0E|B0||Clear the Select channel setting|send only (*2)
0E|B1||Set as select channel|send only (*2); previously set number by CI-V after power ON, or 1 if none selected
0E|B1|01 to 03|Set the channel as a Select channel|01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|B2|00 to 03|Set the Select memory scan channel|send only (*2); 00=ALL 01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|D0||Set Scan resume OFF|send only (*2)
0E|D3||Set Scan resume ON (Close&Delay)|send only (*2)
0F||(none) request, reply 00/01/11/12/13|Read Split / duplex setting|read only (*1); reply 00=Split OFF 01=Split ON 11=DUP- 12=DUP+ 13=DD Repeater Simplex mode (RPS)
0F|00||Set Split function OFF|send only (*2)
0F|01||Set Split function ON|send only (*2)
0F|10||Set the simplex operation|send only (*2)
0F|11||Set DUP- operation|send only (*2)
0F|12||Set DUP+ operation|send only (*2)
0F|13||Set DD Repeater Simplex mode (RPS)|send only (*2)
10||00 to 11|Send/read the tuning step|send/read (*); 00=OFF (10 Hz or 1 Hz),01=100 Hz,02=500 Hz,03=1 kHz,04=5 kHz,05=6.25 kHz,06=10 kHz,07=12.5 kHz,08=20 kHz,09=25 kHz,10=50 kHz,11=100 kHz
11||BCD 1 byte 00 or 10|Send/read attenuator|send/read (*); 00=OFF 10=10 dB attenuator
13|00||Speech all data with voice synthesizer|S meter level, frequency and mode
13|01||Speech the operating frequency and S meter level|
13|02||Speech the operating mode|mode announced after ongoing speech
14|01|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the AF level|send/read (*); 0000=min 0255=max
14|02|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the RF gain level|0000=min 0255=max
14|03|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the squelch level|0000=min 0255=max
14|06|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the NR level|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|07|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read TWIN PBT (PBT1) position|0000=max CCW 0128=center 0255=max CW
14|08|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read TWIN PBT (PBT2) position|0000=max CCW 0128=center 0255=max CW
14|09|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read CW pitch|5 Hz steps; 0000=300 Hz 0128=600 Hz 0255=900 Hz
14|0A|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read RF power|0000=min 0255=max
14|0B|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read MIC gain|0000=min 0255=max
14|0C|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read keying speed|0000=6 WPM 0255=48 WPM
14|0D|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read Notch filter setting|0000=max CCW 0128=center 0255=max CW
14|0E|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the COMP level|0000=0 0255=10
14|0F|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the Break-IN delay|0000=2.0 d 0255=13.0 d
14|12|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read NB level|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|15|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read Monitor audio [MONI] level|0000=0% 0255=100%; NOTE: this model has no 14 14 DRIVE and no 14 13 DIGI-SEL, no 14 05 APF
14|16|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the VOX gain|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|17|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read the Anti VOX gain|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|19|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Send/read LCD backlight brightness|0000=0% 0255=100%
15|01|00 or 01|Read noise or S-meter squelch status|read only (*1); 00=Close 01=Open
15|02|BCD 2 bytes 0000 to 0255|Read S-meter level|0000=S0 0120=S9 0241=S9+60 dB
15|05|00 or 01|Read various squelch (tone squelch etc) status|00=Close 01=Open
15|07|00 or 01|Read the OVF status|00=OVF indicator OFF 01=ON
15|11|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Read the PO meter level|0000=0% 0143=50% 0213=100%
15|12|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Read SWR meter level|0000=SWR1.0 0048=1.5 0080=2.0 0120=3.0
15|13|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Read ALC meter level|0000=min 0120=max
15|14|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Read COMP meter level|0000=0 dB 0130=15 dB 0210=25.5 dB
15|15|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Read Vd meter level|0000=0 V 0013=10 V 0241=16 V
15|16|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Read Id meter level|0000=0 A 0121=10 A 0241=20 A
16|02|00 to 03|Send/read the Preamp / External Preamp|00=P.AMP OFF/EXT-P.AMP OFF 01=P.AMP ON/EXT OFF 02=P.AMP OFF/EXT ON 03=both ON
16|12|01 to 03|Send/read the AGC time constant|01=FAST 02=MID 03=SLOW
16|22|00 or 01|Send/read the Noise blanker|00=OFF 01=ON
16|40|00 or 01|Send/read the Noise reduction|00=OFF 01=ON
16|41|00 or 01|Send/read the Auto Notch function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|42|00 or 01|Send/read the Repeater tone|00=OFF 01=ON
16|43|00 or 01|Send/read the Tone squelch|00=OFF 01=ON
16|44|00 or 01|Send/read the Speech compressor|00=OFF 01=ON
16|45|00 or 01|Send/read the Monitor [MONI] function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|46|00 or 01|Send/read the VOX function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|47|00 to 02|Send/read the BK-IN function|00=BK-IN OFF 01=Semi BK-IN ON 02=Full BK-IN ON
16|48|00 or 01|Send/read the Manual Notch function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|4A|00 or 01|Send/read the AFC function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|4B|00 or 01|Send/read the DTCS function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|4F|00 or 01|Send/read the Twin peak filter|00=OFF 01=ON; ON only when Mark=2125 Hz and Shift=170 Hz
16|50|00 or 01|Send/read the Dial lock function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|56|00 or 01|Send/read the DSP IF filter type|00=SHARP 01=SOFT
16|57|00 to 02|Send/read the Manual Notch width|00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR
16|58|00 to 02|Send/read SSB transmit bandwidth|00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR; applied value depends on COMP: WIDE=1A 05 0017, MID=1A 05 0018, NAR=1A 05 0019
16|59|00 or 01|Send/read the sub band (the Dualwatch function)|00=OFF 01=ON
16|5A|00 or 01|Send/read the satellite mode|00=OFF 01=ON
16|5B|00 to 02|Send/read the DSQL/CSQL setting (DV mode only)|00=OFF 01=DSQL 02=CSQL
16|5C|00 to 02|Set the GPS TX mode|00=OFF 01=D-PRS 02=NMEA
16|(sub byte not printed in the manual; probably 5D - UNSURE)|00 to 03, 06 to 09|Set the Tone squelch function|00=OFF 01=TONE 02=TSQL 03=DTCS 06=DTCS (T) 07=TONE (T)/DTCS (R) 08=DTCS (T)/TSQL (R) 09=TONE (T)/TSQL (R)
16|65|00 or 01|Set the IP Plus function|00=OFF 01=ON
17||ASCII text up to 30 chars (see p.10)|Send CW messages|footnote *3
18|00||Turn OFF the transceiver|
18|01||Turn ON the transceiver|footnote *4
19|00||Read the transceiver ID|read only (*1)
1A|00|see pp.14,15|Send/read memory contents|send/read (*)
1A|01|see p.15|Send/read band stacking register contents|
1A|02|see pp.15,16|Send/read memory keyer contents|footnote *5
1A|03|see p.16|Send/read the selected IF filter width|
1A|04|see p.16|Send/read the selected AGC time constant|
1A|05 00 01|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read SSB RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 02|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read SSB RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 03|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read SSB RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 04|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read AM RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 05|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read AM RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 06|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read AM RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 07|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read FM RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 08|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read FM RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 09|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read FM RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 10|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read DV RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 11|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read DV RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 12|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read Auto DV RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 13|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read CW RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 14|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX > Send/read RTTY RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 15|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read SSB TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 16|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read SSB TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 17|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read SSB TX bandwidth for wide|
1A|05 00 18|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read SSB TX bandwidth for mid|
1A|05 00 19|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read SSB TX bandwidth for narrow|
1A|05 00 20|See p. 16|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > SSB-D TX passband width|
1A|05 00 21|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read AM TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 22|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read AM TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 23|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read FM TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 24|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read FM TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 25|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read DV TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 26|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX > Send/read DV TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5) Cmd. Sub cmd. Data Description
1A|05 00 27|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|SET > Function > Beep Level|(0000=Minimum to 0255=Maximum)
1A|05 00 28|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Beep Level Limit|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 29|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Beep (Confirmation)|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 30|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Band Edge Beep|(00=OFF, 01=ON) ( ON = Beep sounds with a default amateur band) 02 SET > Function > Band Edge Beep (02=ON (User)) 03 SET > Function > Band Edge Beep (03=ON (User) & TX Limit)
1A|05 00 31|BCD 2 bytes 0050 ~ 0200|SET > Function > Beep Sound (MAIN)|(0050=500 Hz to 0200=2000 Hz)
1A|05 00 32|BCD 2 bytes 0050 ~ 0200|SET > Function > Beep Sound (SUB)|(0050=500 Hz to 0200=2000 Hz)
1A|05 00 33|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Sub Band Mute (TX) > Speaker/Phones|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 34|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Sub Band Mute (TX) > USB|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 35|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Sub Band Mute (TX) > LAN|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 36|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > RF/SQL Control|(00=Auto, 01=SQL, 02=RF+SQL)
1A|05 00 37|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > FM/DV Center Error function|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 38|BCD 1 byte 00 to 05|SET > Function > TX Delay > 144M|(00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 39|BCD 1 byte 00 to 05|SET > Function > TX Delay > 430M|(00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 40|BCD 1 byte 00 to 05|SET > Function > TX Delay > 1200M|(00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 41|BCD 1 byte 00 to 05|SET > Function > Time-Out Timer|( 00=OFF, 01=3 min., 02=5 min., 03=10 min., 04=20 min., 05=30 min.)
1A|05 00 42|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > PTT Lock|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 43|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPLIT > Quick SPLIT|(00=OFF, 01=ON) ( Setting the [SPLIT] key operation when it is held down for 1 second.)
1A|05 00 44|See p. 16|SET > Function > SPLIT > FM SPLIT Offset|
1A|05 00 45|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPLIT > SPLIT LOCK|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 46|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Auto Repeater|(00=OFF, 01=ON (DUP,TONE) for USA version)
1A|05 00 47|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > RTTY Mark Frequency|(00=1275 Hz, 01=1615 Hz, 02=2125 Hz)
1A|05 00 48|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > RTTY Shift Width|(00=170 Hz, 01=200 Hz, 02=425 Hz)
1A|05 00 49|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > RTTY Keying Polarity|(00=Normal, 01=Reverse)
1A|05 00 50|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPEECH > SPEECH Language|(00=English, 01=Japanese)
1A|05 00 51|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPEECH > Alphabet|(00=Normal, 01=Phonetic Code)
1A|05 00 52|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPEECH > SPEECH Speed|(00=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 00 53|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > SPEECH > RX Call Sign SPEECH|(00=OFF, 01=ON (Kerchunk), 02=ON (All))
1A|05 00 54|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPEECH > RX>CS SPEECH|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 55|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPEECH > S-Level SPEECH|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 56|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SPEECH > MODE SPEECH|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 57|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|SET > Function > SPEECH > SPEECH Level|(0000=0% to 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 58|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > [SPEECH/LOCK] Switch|(00=SPEECH/LOCK, 01=LOCK/SPEECH)
1A|05 00 59|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Lock Function|(00=MAIN DIAL, 01=PANEL)
1A|05 00 60|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Memo Pad Quantity|(00=5 ch, 01=10 ch)
1A|05 00 61|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > MAIN DIAL Auto TS|(00=OFF, 01=Low, 02=High)
1A|05 00 62|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > MIC Up/Down Speed|(00=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 00 63|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > AFC Limit|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 64|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > [NOTCH] Switch (SSB)|(00=Auto, 01=Manual, 02=Auto/Manual)
1A|05 00 65|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > [NOTCH] Switch (AM)|(00=Auto, 01=Manual, 02=Auto/Manual)
1A|05 00 66|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > SSB/CW Synchronous Tuning|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 67|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > CW Normal Side|(00=LSB, 01=USB)
1A|05 00 68|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Screen Keyboard Type|(00=Ten-key, 01=Full Keyboard)
1A|05 00 69|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Function > Screen Full Keyboard Layout|(00=English, 01=German, 02=French)
1A|05 00 70|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Screen Capture [POWER] Switch|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 71|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Function > Screen Capture File Type|(00=PNG, 01=BMP)
1A|05 00 72|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|SET > Function > REF Adjust|(0000=0%, 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 73|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|SET > Function > REF Adjust (FINE)|(0000=0%, 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 74|BCD 1 byte 00 to 03|SET > DV/DD Set > Standby Beep|( 00=OFF, 01=ON, 02=ON (to me: High Tone), 03=ON (to me: Alarm/High Tone))
1A|05 00 75|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > DV/DD Set > Auto Reply|(00=OFF, 01=ON, 02=Voice)
1A|05 00 76|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > DV Data TX|(00=PTT 01=Auto)
1A|05 00 77|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > DV Fast Data > Fast Data|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 78|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > DV Fast Data > GPS Data Speed|(00=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 00 79|BCD 1 byte 00 to 10|SET > DV/DD Set > DV Fast Data > TX Delay (PTT)|(00=OFF, 01=1 sec. to 10=10 sec.)
1A|05 00 80|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > DV/DD Set > Digital Monitor|(00=Auto, 01=Digital, 02=Analog)
1A|05 00 81|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > Digital Repeater Set|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 82|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > DV Auto Detect|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 83|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > RX Record (RPT)|(00=ALL, 01=Latest Only)
1A|05 00 84|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > BK|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 85|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > EMR|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 86|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|SET > DV/DD Set > EMR AF Level|(0000=0%, 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 87|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > DD TX Inhibit (Power ON)|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 88|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > DV/DD Set > DD Packet Output|(00=Normal, 01=All)
1A|05 00 89|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > QSO/RX Log > QSO Log|(00=OFF, 01=ON) Cmd. Sub cmd. Data Description
1A|05 00 90|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > QSO/RX Log > RX History Log|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 91|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > QSO/RX Log > CSV Format > Separator/Decimal|( 00=Separator is " , " and Decimal is " . ," 01=Separator is " ; " and Decimal is " . ," 02=Separator is " ; " and Decimal is " , ")
1A|05 00 92|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > QSO/RX Log > CSV Format > Date|(00="yyyy/mm/dd," 01="mm/dd/yyyy," 02="dd/mm/yyyy")
1A|05 00 93|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Connectors > External P.AMP > 144M|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 94|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Connectors > External P.AMP > 430M|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 95|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Connectors > External P.AMP > 1200M|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 96|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Connectors > External Speaker Separate|(00=Separate, 01=Mix)
1A|05 00 97|BCD 1 byte 00 to 30|SET > Connectors > Phones > Level|(00=-15 dB to 30=+15 dB)
1A|05 00 98|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|SET > Connectors > Phones > L/R Mix|(00=Separate, 01=Mix, 02=Auto)
1A|05 00 99|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > AF/SQL Output Select|(00=MAIN, 01=SUB)
1A|05 01 00|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|SET > Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > Output Select|(00=AF, 01=IF)
